WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Welcome to the video on exploring B2B product recommendations.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000
At Amazon, we can't always predict exactly what business customers will buy,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
but we collect data, analyze trends, and share recommendations with professional sellers

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.500
to help take the guesswork out of listing and pricing B2B products on Amazon.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.500
We offer new product recommendations to business sellers each week on Seller Central.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.500
If you're a professional seller, you can access them anytime by clicking B2B from the main menu

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.000
and selecting Product Opportunities.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
On the B2B Product Opportunities page, or BPO,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.000
you can examine two types of recommendations using the tabs at the top of the screen.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.143
Recommended for you includes products that are in high demand from categories and brands you

00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:47.000
already sell.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Products not yet on Amazon include those requested by Amazon business customers

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.000
that may not yet be available on Amazon.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.769
The products listed on the Recommended for You tab

00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:03.091
are generated by combining demand signals from Amazon business customers with your current product

00:01:03.091 --> 00:01:03.500
listings.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.750
You can create an offer for one of the top 10 recommendations by clicking the Sell Yours

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:14.167
button to the right of a product, or you can click the Generate Your Report button to view

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:15.500
up to 1,000 recommendations.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.556
On the Products Not Yet on Amazon tab, you'll find a list of items

00:01:20.556 --> 00:01:26.714
that have been requested by Amazon business customers, but which don't yet have ASINs or

00:01:26.714 --> 00:01:29.000
Amazon standard identification numbers.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.692
Missing ASINs suggest these products aren't currently

00:01:31.692 --> 00:01:37.000
listed on Amazon, which means you could be the first seller to meet a new demand.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:37.900
If you want to

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:43.500
add a product not yet on Amazon, click the Add Product button on the right side of the screen.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.167
If you want to see additional products without ASINs that have been requested by

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:53.962
business buyers, click the Generate Downloadable Report button and get up to 1,000 product recommendations,

00:01:53.962 --> 00:01:59.500
along with product categories and the industries of customers making the requests.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.559
Note that both

00:02:00.559 --> 00:02:06.571
the products not yet on Amazon report and the Recommended for You report can take up to 10 minutes

00:02:06.571 --> 00:02:07.000
to generate.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.200
If you automate your business on Amazon, both these reports are also available

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.000
through the Reports API.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.077
Navigate to the GitHub Reports Reference folder and scroll to Amazon

00:02:19.077 --> 00:02:20.000
Business Reports.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.417
Whether you're new to B2B products or sell regularly to Amazon business customers,

00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:31.000
B2B product opportunities can help you meet the demands of those buying for work.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Explore this resource and others anytime by clicking B2B in the main menu on Seller Central.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:43.000
This concludes our video on exploring B2B product recommendations.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Thank you, and happy selling on Amazon.
